<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n112004" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φοίνιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ος</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			Pi.
			<u>I.</u>
			4(3).35(53)
		</span></i>:—poet.Adj., used for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φόνιος,</span> when the first syll. is to be long, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of</i> or <i>like blood,
				blood-red,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἷμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					18.97
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Th.</u>
				737
			</span></i>(lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				783
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δρόσος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					1390
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φ. στάλαγμα,</span> i. e. blood,
				<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				1239
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>bloody, blood-stained,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φ. ἀλκά,</span> of Ajax, Pi.l.c.;
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φ. ξυνωρίς,</span> prob. of public and
			private loss, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				643
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χεὶρ φ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Aj.</u>
					772
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χεῖρες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>OT</u>
					466
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κοπίς</span> prob. for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κόνις</span> in <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				601
			</span></i> (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>bloody, murderous,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σκύλλα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ch.</u>
					614
				</span></i>
			(lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέπληγμαι . .
			δήγματι</span> (prob. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δάκει</span>)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc"> φοινίῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					1164
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				1278
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φ. Ἄρης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>El.</u>
					96
				</span></i>
			 (anap.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔχιδνα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					770
				</span></i>
			: metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φ. σάλος,</span> of
			pestilence, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>OT</u>
				24
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Aj.</u>
				352
			</span></i>.—Rare in Com., <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Th.</u>
				694
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
